{{also|Sepsis|sépsis}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|σῆψις||putrefaction}}, from {{m|grc|σήπειν||to make rotten}}, from {{m|grc|σήψ||a kind of lizard; also a kind of serpent whose bite was alleged to cause putrefaction}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛpsɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|sepses}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A serious medical [[condition]] in which the whole body is inflamed, causing injury to its own tissues and organs as a response to infection.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|antiseptic}}
* {{l|en|asepsis}}
* {{l|en|aseptic}}
* {{l|en|septic}}
* {{l|en|septicemia}}
* {{l|en|septicity}}

